<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?>
<!-- What the resource shrinker must not take.

     This list was written after a release build dropped @drawable/splash and the app died on launch with
     Resources.NotFoundException — "Puzzle keeps stopping", on every open, only in the shipped build. The cause
     was that the Trusted Web Activity named the splash from a manifest <meta-data android:resource="...">,
     and shrinkResources does not walk those.

     The splash is Android's own now, and its brains are named from the Theme.App.Starting styles, which the
     shrinker does follow — the night and mint ones only through styles that code names at run time
     (MainActivity.rememberTheme), which it follows too. So this file is a belt to those braces rather than the
     only thing holding the splash in. It stays because the failure it prevents is invisible in debug builds
     and fatal in release ones, and because the colours below are still partly referenced from places the walk
     does not reach.

     ic_stat_puzzle is here for the original reason: the manifest names it as Firebase's default notification
     icon through the same kind of meta-data that lost the splash. Code names it too, which the shrinker does
     see, but a notification that arrives with no icon is a crash in the shipped build and nowhere else. -->
<resources xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    tools:keep="@drawable/splash_mark,@drawable/splash_mark_night,@drawable/splash_mark_mint,@drawable/ic_stat_puzzle,@color/paper,@color/ink,@color/paper_night,@color/ink_night,@color/paper_mint,@color/ink_mint" />
